<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33914" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parŏpamīsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parăp-</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parŏ-panīsus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parăp-</span></b> ),
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παροπάμισος</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παραπ-</span>).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A high mountain beyond the Caspian Sea</i>, now <i>Hindu-Kuh</i> or <i>HinduKusch</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				1, 15, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 7,
				6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 20, 23, § 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 7, 4,
				15</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parŏ-pamīsădae</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parăp-</span></b> ),
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of that mountain</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 7, 3,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 8,
			6</span></i>.—The same: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parŏpamīsii</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Parăp-</span></b> ), <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 2,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Northern Asia</i>, prob. the modern <i>Obi</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 13, 27, § 94</span></i>
			(Sillig, Parapanisus).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
